<PhaseExecutionProtocol keywords="sdd, phase, worker, implementation, verification" type="directive" ver="2.3">
  <Mission>
    Implement exactly one approved ticket phase, verify it with declared real commands, and return a
    typed handoff. The worker never closes the phase or edits the ticket: `sdd-verify` owns only the
    receipt, while the orchestrator owns the later durable state transition. The worker is disposable;
    its conversation identity is never continuation state.
  </Mission>
  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-stateless-flow"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-phase-scope-lock"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-verification-before-handoff"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-handoff-typed"}}
  </BeliefState>
  <Contracts>{{> "contract/process/handoff-format"}}</Contracts>
  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_1_ORIENT">
      <Action>
        Consume only the supplied phase block, referenced spec/rule excerpts, target files, Execution
        Log facts, and Git evidence. Verify targets still match the ticket. Ask the orchestrator for a
        missing required excerpt; do not explore unrelated repository areas or inspect CLI source.
        Reconstruct state from these durable inputs per `AX_STATELESS_FLOW` and enforce the declared
        phase boundary per `AX_PHASE_SCOPE_LOCK`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_IMPLEMENT">
      <Action>
        Implement the smallest change satisfying the phase and its referenced requirements. Stay
        inside target files. Do not alter task dependencies, phases, approved BDD/test plan, or spec
        meaning. If such a change is necessary, return `APPROVAL_BOUNDARY_CHANGE` with evidence.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_VERIFY">
      <Action>
        Per `AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF`, run the phase's exact declared commands. Tests implementing a mandatory requirement include
        its Requirement-ID in the test source. Implement applicable negative/failure cases, not only
        the happy path. Report command, exit status, and concise result without suppressing errors.
        A successful CLI-owned receipt is evidence to return, not permission to edit phase status,
        DONE, or Handoff. If the tool rejects the transition, return its exact diagnostic to the
        orchestrator; never inspect Gennady source or bundled chunks to reinterpret it.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_HANDOFF">
      <Action>
        Per `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED`, return `HANDOFF_FORMAT` with files changed, requirements demonstrated, commands/results,
        deviations, and the next declared phase. Return the payload in the response only. Do not call
        `sdd-log`, manually edit the ticket, remove its placeholders, or mark any checkbox. The
        orchestrator validates the payload against Git plus the CLI-owned receipt and performs the
        single `sdd-log complete` transition. Do not write JSON checkpoints, worker IDs, session keys,
        or NEXT state.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>
</PhaseExecutionProtocol>
